# Security — DevSecOps & AppSec

Source: [security-devsecops-ssdls-appsec](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Secrets & config
- Never hardcode API keys, JWT secrets, or provider tokens
- No `.env` or credentials in git; use environment variables
- Never log secrets, session tokens, or full tool-call payloads containing PII

## Input & output
- Validate all ingest payloads via Pydantic; sanitize displayed user/agent content in UI (XSS)
- Parameterized queries / ORM only — no string-built SQL
- Treat red-team attack templates as untrusted content in the UI (escape, don't `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`)

## Auth & authorization
- Enforce tenant scoping via `X-API-Key` / auth middleware on containment API
- Least privilege for agent tool policies and org YAML rules
- Rate-limit ingest and campaign endpoints

## Dependencies
- Pin versions in `pyproject.toml` / `package.json`
- Prefer well-maintained packages; note new deps in PR description

## AI-specific
- LLM judge outputs are untrusted — validate structured JSON before persisting
- Containment verdicts must not auto-execute destructive actions without explicit action enum (`KILL`, `QUARANTINE`)
- Benchmark datasets must not contain real customer data

## Compliance alignment
- Map findings to OWASP LLM Top 10 and MITRE ATLAS where applicable
- Document security controls in API/export surfaces for audit trails
